    "recommendations": "• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective address numbers visible from the road in both directions.\n• Keep the access drive clear of parked vehicles to allow fire apparatus to reach the main residence and detached structure without obstruction.\n• Mark or designate a turnaround area near the detached structure so responding crews do not need to back out to the road.\n• Keep the walkway between the main residence and detached structure clear to allow responders to move on foot between structures quickly.\n• Install a reflective address marker at the detached structure identifying it as a separate building on the property.\n• Keep the access drive surface in condition that supports the weight of fire apparatus and ambulances year-round.\n• Confirm the access drive width is sufficient to allow an apparatus to pass a parked vehicle without stopping."
