    "recommendations": "• Clear grass and low vegetation from directly around the base of the house and any outbuildings.\n• Thin scattered shrubs near structures to increase open space between plants and buildings.\n• Trim lower branches on trees closest to the house to reduce the path fire can travel from ground vegetation up into the tree canopy.\n• Mow or cut grass across the property regularly, especially during dry periods, to keep it short and reduce the amount of burnable material near the house.\n• Keep the single access route clear of overhanging branches and encroaching shrubs so vehicles can move through without obstruction.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is easy to locate quickly from the road.\n• Clear vegetation along the rear of the property to create a path that allows movement around the back of the house.\n• Remove any dead grass, dry plant material, or debris that has collected near the foundation, under decks, or against exterior walls.\n• Separate any wood piles, outdoor furniture, or stored materials from the exterior walls of the house."
